 directed hypergraph’s matrix this way (aᵢⱼ = −1 for a tail node, 1 for a head","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"node); a directed graph’s edge is the column with one source and one target, the matrix of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"spectral graph theory (B·Bᵀ = L, Godsil–Royle §8.3) and NetworkX’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidence_matrix(oriented=True)"},{"text":". It conforms to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedHypergraph"},{"text":", so the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraphs"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"algorithms (B- and F-connection, components, the clique expansion) run on it unchanged; it is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"title":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/documentation\/IncidenceMatrixModule\/OrientedIncidenceMatrix","url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix","type":"topic","kind":"symbol"},"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/OrientedIncidenceMatrix/description":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The shape, then the rows as strings of ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-"},{"text":" (−1), ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"+"},{"text":" (+1), column 0 leftmost, at","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"most 16 rows of 64 columns: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"3×2 [-0, +-, 0+]"},{"text":". The empty matrix is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0×0 []"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/orientedincidencematrix\/description","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IncidenceMatrix